  "details": "I would like to request friend-specific presence privacy controls.\n\nCurrently, status and joinability settings apply broadly. However, VRChat users often belong to multiple friend groups or communities, and they may not always want every friend group to see the same presence information.\n\nFor example, while I am spending time with Friend A or one social circle, I may want Friend B or another group to see me as unavailable, private, or not joinable.\n\nRequested feature:\n\nAllow users to choose how they appear to selected friends or custom friend lists.\n\nPossible options:\n\n- Show normal status\n\n- Show as Orange\n\n- Show as Red\n\n- Show as “In a private instance”\n\n- Show as “Unavailable”\n\n- Hide detailed join information\n\n- Hide instance type or joinability\n\nThis would not block, unfriend, or ban anyone. It would only change how the user’s presence and joinability are shown to selected people.\n\nWhy this matters:\n\nCurrent options are too broad. Changing status affects everyone, while blocking or unfriending is too strong for ordinary social boundaries.\n\nFriend-specific presence privacy would help users manage different friend groups and communities without unnecessary social pressure, conflict, or moderation actions.",
